Licensing guidance
==================

The MIT license above covers the game's source code. For a commercial Steam
release you may wish to:

- Keep source under MIT (or dual-license) while shipping the compiled game under
  a separate end-user license agreement (see docs/STEAM.md for a EULA template
  that must be reviewed by a lawyer before use).
- Replace the placeholder generated art/audio with your own commissioned assets
  and license those separately (see docs/ASSET_REPLACEMENT.md).
- If you bundle a dyslexia-friendly font, include that font's own license file
  and confirm redistribution is permitted. This project uses a safe system-font
  fallback by default and bundles no third-party font.
